<%/* /legal: moved from public/legal.html. Shared blocks, prices and contact details come from it.blocks and it.t. */%>
<% layout('/layouts/base', {
  meta: {
    "title": "Legal & Company Details | VERGO Staffing",
    "description": "Vergo Ltd's company registration, regulatory status and insurance details.",
    "ogImage": "/images/og/home.jpg",
    "canonical": "/legal"
  }
}) %>
    <section class="page-hero-plain shell">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1>Company and regulatory details</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated 26 September 2026.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight shell legal-content">
      <h2>1. Company details</h2>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>Legal name: <%~ it.t.LEGAL_NAME %>, trading as VERGO Staffing</li>
        <li>Registered in: England and Wales</li>
        <li>Company number: <%~ it.t.COMPANY_NUMBER %></li>
        <li>Registered office: <%~ it.t.REGISTERED_OFFICE %></li>
        <li>Contact: <a href="mailto:<%~ it.t.EMAIL %>"><%~ it.t.EMAIL %></a>, <a href="<%~ it.t.PHONE_TEL %>"><%~ it.t.PHONE %></a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. Regulatory status</h2>
      <p>Vergo Ltd operates as an employment business, supplying workers to clients under contracts for services. We're subject to:</p>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>The Employment Agencies Act 1973</li>
        <li>The Conduct of Employment Agencies and Employment Businesses Regulations 2003, which govern how we deal with clients ("hirers") and workers ("work-seekers"), including the restriction on charging work-seekers for finding them work, and the rules on transfer fees covered in our <a href="/terms">terms of business</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p>The Employment Rights Act 2025 is changing rules for agency and zero-hours workers in stages through 2026 and 2027. We'll update these terms as each change takes effect.</p>
      <p>Enforcement of these regulations is moving to the Fair Work Agency, a new single enforcement body. This doesn't change our obligations, only who checks them.</p>

      <h2>3. Insurance</h2>
      <p>We hold employers' liability and public liability insurance. Certificates are available on request.</p>
      <%~ it.blocks["legal-insurers"]() %>

      <h2>4. Data protection</h2>
      <%~ it.blocks["legal-ico"]() %>
      <p>See our <a href="/privacy">privacy notice</a> for how we handle personal data.</p>

      <h2>5. Complaints</h2>
      <p>If something's gone wrong, contact us directly at <a href="mailto:<%~ it.t.EMAIL %>"><%~ it.t.EMAIL %></a> or <a href="<%~ it.t.PHONE_TEL %>"><%~ it.t.PHONE %></a>. We aim to acknowledge complaints within 5 working days.</p>

      <h2>6. Governing law</h2>
      <p>These pages and our dealings with clients and workers are governed by the law of England and Wales.</p>
    </section>
